    "reasoning": "All 16 mathematical answers agree with their own captured MA worked solutions. Confirmation rests on those solutions; no grades were supplied. q-29885 and q-103593: apply the power rule and integrate 1/x as ln|x|. q-10871: the tangent slope is 5, so the normal is y-3=-(x-1)/5 and its x-intercept is (16,0). q-103546: the tangent slope is -2, giving normal x-2y=-7; hence p=-2, q=-7 and q-p=-5. For completing the square, use au²+bu+c=a(u+b/(2a))²+c-b²/(4a). This gives the selected expressions for q-141527, q-141536, q-141552, q-140410, q-140330, q-52522, q-52537, q-35079 and q-140378; expanding each recovers its original polynomial. q-141817 reduces to (y-4)²=4/5, giving y=4±2/√5. q-141811 reduces to (x+3)²=25/4, giving x=-11/2 or -1/2. q-112524 becomes 4(x+3/4)²=29/4, so p+q=8. The source's alignment markers and grouping braces do not change the values of the matching current choices. In q-35079 and q-140378, the prose refers to constant terms 8 and 1 while the displayed terms are -8 and -1; the subsequent calculations and final answers correctly preserve those negative signs.",
